      "description": "Space Shuttle Endeavor seen in its temporary exhibit at the California Science Center in Los Angeles, California. The shuttle has been displayed in this temporary building since being delivered to the science center in October 2012. Currently, construction is underway for the permanent exhibit which will display the shuttle outside and upright, along with the two solid rocket boosters (SRBs) and external tank (ET). It will appear as it would on the launch pad at Kennedy Space Center.\nThe external tank has been delivered to the science center and currently stored outside on its side, immediately north of the temporary shuttle building.",
